<!-- ── Intro Box ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<blockquote>
<strong>🧠 Think of it this way:</strong> <code>AgentState</code> is like a <em>shared whiteboard in a meeting room</em>. Nineteen analysts walk in, each writes their findings in their own designated section, and the portfolio manager reads all sections before making a decision. Nobody erases anyone else's notes — the <code>merge_dicts</code> reducer guarantees that. The <strong>LLM factory</strong> is like a <em>universal TV remote</em> that works with any brand: you press one button (<code>get_model()</code>), specify the brand (<code>ModelProvider.OPENAI</code>), and get a working controller — no need to learn each brand's proprietary interface.
</blockquote>

